<title>INDIA: INDIA SEBI TO DISCUSS CARRY-FORWARD ON SEPTEMBER 5.</title>
<headline>INDIA SEBI TO DISCUSS CARRY-FORWARD ON SEPTEMBER 5.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) will consider reforms in carry-forward trade at a meeting in Madras on September 5, its chairman D.R. Mehta told a news conference on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Please take my word for it,&quot; Mehta said. &quot;It was not considered today, it has been deferred.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91)-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
